# FRPB — Repository root environment template (monorepo).
#
# This is a POINTER file. The application configuration lives per app:
#
#   apps/web/.env.example      -> the complete web (Next.js) variable set.
#                                 Copy to apps/web/.env and fill in.
#   apps/desktop/.env.example  -> desktop-local overrides, if any (usually none;
#                                 the desktop reads VITE_* values at build time
#                                 and its license endpoint at runtime).
#
# Nothing at the repository root is read at runtime by either app, which is why
# this file intentionally contains no secrets or live values.
#
# ── Quick start ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   cp apps/web/.env.example apps/web/.env
#   # then fill in the blanks
#
# ── Variable names must match the code exactly ──────────────────────────────
# A renamed payment key does not crash the app; it makes checkout return a 502
# "not configured". Use the names from apps/web/.env.example verbatim.
#
# ── Supported payment rails (only two) ──────────────────────────────────────
#   INR / domestic India  -> Cashfree   (CASHFREE_CLIENT_ID, CASHFREE_CLIENT_SECRET)
#   USD / international   -> PayGlocal  (PAYGLOCAL_MERCHANT_ID, PAYGLOCAL_MERCHANT_KEY,
#                                        PAYGLOCAL_MERCHANT_SECRET)
# Stripe and Razorpay were removed from the codebase.
#
# ── Required at minimum to boot ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, DATABASE_URL
#
# Everything else degrades gracefully: missing gateway keys disable that rail
# (the other still works), missing RESEND_API_KEY skips email, and absent
# Upstash credentials fall back to in-memory rate limiting.
#
# See apps/web/.env.example for the full annotated list.
